  "source": "Amazon Bedrock ListFoundationModels/ListInferenceProfiles for us-east-1, read 2026-10-03; Converse support from the Bedrock API compatibility table",
  "notes": [
    "Claude Opus 5.5 is back on the global inference profile (AWS advice 2026-10-07: use global, not us.): on 2026-10-07 the production instance role got 8 of 8 answers from global.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5 in about 1.3 s (the 2026-10-05 ServiceUnavailableException is gone); the instance role still allows the us. profile and its routed models. Claude Fable 5 and 5.1 were withdrawn on 2026-10-07: Bedrock keeps all Fable traffic for up to 30 days for AWS review (the aws_review retention setting), which AwwO does not accept for user content.",
    "target is the Converse modelId: a system inference profile (global./us.) where the model is only offered through one, otherwise the in-region model id.",
    "contextWindow and maxTokens are AwwO's conservative budgets (the workers treat contextWindow as a byte budget), not provider maxima.",
    "tools is true only where a streamed tool call was observed or the model card documents ConverseStream tool use; models without it run on Pi only. Pixtral Large and the Llama models take tools only in non-streaming Converse (ConverseStream answers \"This model doesn't support tool use in streaming mode\"), so they run on Pi.",
    "verified names the date a real ConverseStream call through the AwwO workers answered from this account (2026-10-04: with the production instance role); an empty value means the model is not offered yet: AWS Marketplace refused its subscription (INVALID_PAYMENT_INSTRUMENT).",
    "fallbackTarget is the same model through its other inference profile (global. <-> us.), with its own capacity and quotas: the bridge tries it once, on the same client, when the target refuses a call for capacity or quota (ThrottlingException, ServiceUnavailableException, InternalServerException, ModelNotReadyException, ServiceQuotaExceededException) before anything streamed. On 2026-10-19 global Claude Haiku 4.5 answered ServiceUnavailableException 17 times and global Claude Opus 5.5 hit its daily token quota (which the account's other Bedrock users share) while the us. profiles answered; the workers' IAM user may call both profiles since then.",
    "proseBytesPerToken is the model's measured bytes of prose per token (apps/context-estimate.ts): on 2026-10-21 each model read 16 texts through the production workers (Chinese, English, a Chinese canvas as JSON, code, HTML/CSS, Markdown, Japanese/Korean, emoji chat, and the dense ones: CSV, tool traffic, base64, short-key JSON, minified code, SVG paths, server logs, URLs), and the rate is the largest that covers every text's reported input tokens with the prose part counted 15% denser (.local/calib/fit2.py of the context-limit session). Dense text counts byte for byte whatever the rate. A model without one (not measured) keeps the byte rule."
  ],
